1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:04,294
This is an office building, owned
through a commercial property fund.

2
00:00:04,294 --> 00:00:07,768
Its register of owners is
kept during business hours.

3
00:00:07,868 --> 00:00:13,863
Tokenisation records ownership as digital tokens,
and lets you program the rules of the asset.

4
00:00:13,863 --> 00:00:16,063
The fund stays a unit trust.

5
00:00:16,163 --> 00:00:17,684
Step one, set up.

6
00:00:17,684 --> 00:00:23,669
The fund manager verifies the entity, adds the
fund details, and sets the rules on who can hold.

7
00:00:23,669 --> 00:00:27,370
Those rules are encoded into
the token's smart contract.

8
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:29,105
Step two, investors.

9
00:00:29,105 --> 00:00:33,255
Each investor completes identity
checks and investor classification.

10
00:00:33,255 --> 00:00:35,820
No verified wallet, no tokens.

11
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:37,476
Step three, issue.

12
00:00:37,476 --> 00:00:41,783
Tokens are minted on Redbelly
Network and sent to verified wallets.

13
00:00:41,783 --> 00:00:46,418
Each is a fractional ownership interest,
and the register updates immediately.

14
00:00:46,518 --> 00:00:48,129
Step four, transfer.

15
00:00:48,129 --> 00:00:51,103
Every transfer is checked against the rules first.

16
00:00:51,103 --> 00:00:56,778
A transfer to an ineligible investor is
rejected. A compliant one settles in seconds.

17
00:00:56,878 --> 00:01:01,720
Distributions are paid to verified
wallets in a single on-chain transaction.

18
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:06,011
Records stay current for
administrators, auditors and regulators.

19
00:01:06,111 --> 00:01:11,124
The fund manager uses a familiar platform,
with no blockchain expertise required.

20
00:01:11,124 --> 00:01:16,576
Underneath runs Redbelly Network, Australia's
public digital token infrastructure.

21
00:01:16,676 --> 00:01:21,825
One building, one fund, now a compliant
token on Redbelly Network, through Tokeniser.

22
00:01:21,825 --> 00:01:24,208
Learn more at tokeniser dot com.
